You can make a stew in five minutes, cut it into small pieces and put it in a soup, or cut it into small pieces and put it in a salad, and you can take it out right away and use it easily.

228
00:24:11,217 --> 00:24:16,283
Pumpkin doesn't taste good when frozen, so we don't do it in our house.

229
00:24:17,283 --> 00:24:25,617
We put them in storage containers like this and eat them up in 3 or 4 days.

230
00:24:26,783 --> 00:24:35,083
Now, the cabbage is removed only from the outer leaves that are sore, and lightly washed.

231
00:24:35,783 --> 00:24:39,250
I'm going to let it sleep until the weekend.

232
00:24:39,617 --> 00:24:48,750
Use a small knife to hollow out the core. Because the core absorbs nutrients from the leaves and shrivels up.

233
00:24:49,117 --> 00:24:52,183
in the hollowed out part.

234
00:24:52,517 --> 00:24:58,117
Press a wet dish towel into the hollowed-out area

235
00:24:59,050 --> 00:25:05,750
I wrap it in newspaper to prevent condensation, and then I put it in a bag, but I don't have any newspaper.

236
00:25:06,117 --> 00:25:19,950
I store them in a double layer of washed and dried bags.

237
00:25:20,350 --> 00:25:31,450
Two small carrots bought cheap, cut into small pieces.

238
00:25:35,083 --> 00:25:41,583
Put them in a stasher

239
00:25:41,950 --> 00:25:45,583
If you freeze it as it is, it makes soup life easier every day.

240
00:25:45,950 --> 00:25:51,450
Oh, and watch the previous video about soup life.

241
00:25:52,317 --> 00:25:54,883
One cucumber is made into a pickle.

242
00:25:55,450 --> 00:25:58,717
This is our small bed of rice bran

243
00:25:59,117 --> 00:26:12,117
Cucumbers pickled the day before are taken out and the bran is washed off

244
00:26:13,083 --> 00:26:17,450
Stir well

245
00:26:17,783 --> 00:26:22,517
New cucumbers I N!

246
00:26:22,917 --> 00:26:31,183
I recommend my nakudoko because fermented foods are good for you, easy to make, and delicious!

247
00:26:31,683 --> 00:26:39,950
