248
00:26:49,317 --> 00:26:53,417
See also the extra video on how to preserve ginger...

249
00:26:53,817 --> 00:27:06,817
You can keep it for a couple of weeks if you put it in a stasher and soak it in water.

250
00:27:07,717 --> 00:27:14,650
This is how garlic is stored

251
00:27:15,283 --> 00:27:20,483
Buy in bulk and put straight into the stasher without peeling

252
00:27:20,950 --> 00:27:26,650
By the way, these are for immediate use in the refrigerator. They will last 3-4 weeks depending on freshness.

253
00:27:27,017 --> 00:27:33,550
These are frozen. If fresh, it will last more than 6 months.

254
00:27:34,050 --> 00:27:40,017
By the way, if you are a stasher, you don't have to wrap each one individually.

255
00:27:40,383 --> 00:27:47,350
And it doesn't freeze inside. You can cut the buttocks with a little bit of light force.

256
00:27:47,683 --> 00:27:52,283
And then soak it in water for about 5 minutes to thaw it out.

257
00:27:52,650 --> 00:28:01,583
And the skin comes off easily like this.

258
00:28:02,417 --> 00:28:07,317
If you freeze them chopped or grated, they don't taste good because they get freezer burn.

259
00:28:07,750 --> 00:28:12,883
This is the recommended way to store them for a long time and use them deliciously

260
00:28:13,617 --> 00:28:19,550
Preparation of bought vegetables - it's done!

261
00:28:20,183 --> 00:28:23,817
An hour's hard work of buying the food will make a week's cooking easier

262
00:28:24,250 --> 00:28:27,517
I freeze what I don't use right away.

263
00:28:27,883 --> 00:28:30,183
If you store them upright in the vegetable compartment, they will last up to a week.

264
00:28:30,550 --> 00:28:34,950
Prepared for immediate use, it keeps the refrigerator clean and easy to remove.

265
00:28:35,283 --> 00:28:40,483
Red, green, yellow, and various colored foods can be easily incorporated in a well-balanced way.

266
00:28:40,850 --> 00:28:45,717
Corn is also ready to eat after thawing at room temperature. It can be used for cooking or as a snack if you are hungry.

267
00:28:46,083 --> 00:28:51,017
Just shove whatever vegetables you have left over into the rice bran - lol!

268
00:28:51,383 --> 00:28:55,817
I cut leafy greens into small, easy-to-use pieces so I can take them out and use them right away.

269
00:29:00,717 --> 00:29:06,350
Cover them with a wet cloth so that condensation water doesn't fall on the leaves.

270
00:29:09,917 --> 00:29:13,417
You should know what's in it, so you don't forget to use it.

271
00:29:14,050 --> 00:29:17,150
Put cabbage in the vegetable room with the roots facing down.

272
00:29:17,483 --> 00:29:20,650
Cucumbers and carrots are stored upright

273
00:29:21,017 --> 00:29:24,783
Remember, leafy greens are in enameled containers

274
00:29:25,117 --> 00:29:31,417
No leakage of water if you put bean sprouts in a stasher

275
00:29:31,817 --> 00:29:37,750
You can put leafy greens, broccoli, etc. in the top shelf, too.

276
